Agent corpus — drop documents here.
===================================

Anything you put in this folder becomes retrievable by the triage agent, which
cites it by filename in its briefs. Until something lands here, briefs are
written from live signals alone and carry no citations; that is a normal,
handled state, not an error (see twin/agent/rag.py).

What is read
------------
Files ending in .md, .txt or .json, at any depth below this folder.
Everything else -- including this README, which deliberately has no extension --
is ignored, so notes to yourself never end up quoted in an incident brief.

What is worth putting here
--------------------------
  * Standard operating procedures for flood, fire, heat and crowd incidents
  * Escalation matrices: who is called, at what threshold, in what order
  * Past situation reports, so the agent can point at how a similar day went
  * Shelter, hospital and depot registers as .json

After adding or removing files
------------------------------
The index is cached in-process. Restart the server, or call
twin.agent.rag.reset_index(), before the new documents are retrievable.
The embedding model runs locally; no API key is involved.

Configure the location with TWIN_RAG_CORPUS_DIR if you keep documents elsewhere.
